From b77d22e44e6c56240fda5b04fd0d790bd3ddf0dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:10:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kk: sparse binding and residency with Metal 4 placement
 sparse resources

Sparse buffers and images are Metal placement sparse buffers/textures
(private, MTLSparsePageSize64) whose 64 KiB pages vkQueueBindSparse maps
from placement heaps with MTL4CommandQueue updateBufferMappings /
updateTextureMappings, after the submit's waits and before its signals.
Encoders wait for the queue's resource state stage when sparse binding is
enabled; earlier encoders already end with a barrier before all queue
stages, so unmapping waits for prior work.

- Memory: sparse resources only bind the device-local type (memory type 0):
  its allocations are never host pointer imports (virglrenderer imports
  host-visible memory) and get heaps with
  maxCompatiblePlacementSparsePageSize 64 KiB.
- Images: 2D, single-sample, optimal, non depth/stencil formats whose Metal
  64 KiB tile equals the Vulkan standard 2D block shape (all 8-128 bit and
  BC formats on Apple GPUs) -> residencyStandard2DBlockShape. Opaque binds
  address per layer the tiles of each level below Metal's mip tail, then
  Metal's tail. The Vulkan mip tail starts at the first level smaller than a
  tile (no ALIGNED_MIP_SIZE): Metal's tail starts below half a tile, the
  levels in between are tiles inside the Vulkan tail region. One tail per
  layer. GPU-optimized (compressed) contents are off for sparse images so
  aliases see the same data.
- Unmapped pages read zero (alpha one for formats without alpha, i.e. a
  zero-filled image) and drop writes (MTLTextureSparseTier1,
  MTLBufferSparseTier1) -> residencyNonResidentStrict.
- 3D sparse tiles are 2D-shaped in Metal (not the standard 3D blocks), no
  sparse MSAA: sparseResidencyImage3D and the sample count features stay
  off.

Needs MTLDevice.supportsPlacementSparse (all Apple7 Macs and later).
